# Day 58 – Active Directory DNS Troubleshooting & Windows 11 Client Preparation

## 🎯 Objective

Today's objective was to continue building the Active Directory home lab by troubleshooting DNS on the Domain Controller and preparing the Windows 11 client for Active Directory domain connectivity.

The main focus was understanding the difference between:

* Internal Active Directory DNS resolution
* External Internet DNS resolution
* DNS forwarding
* Client DNS configuration
* Domain Controller connectivity
* Active Directory domain-join preparation

A real troubleshooting issue was identified where the Active Directory domain could be resolved successfully, but external hostnames such as `google.com` could not be resolved. The issue was investigated and resolved by configuring DNS forwarders on the Domain Controller.

