# 🧠 Important DNS Concept Learned

Today's troubleshooting reinforced an important distinction:

```text
DNS is working
≠
All DNS queries are working
```

A DNS server may successfully resolve internal Active Directory records while failing to resolve external Internet names.

For example:

```text
kpatel.test
   ↓
Internal DNS
   ↓
SUCCESS
```

but:

```text
google.com
   ↓
External DNS forwarding
   ↓
FAILURE
```

This is why DNS troubleshooting should test both internal and external resolution.

