# 🔑 Key Takeaways

### 1. Internal and external DNS are different troubleshooting areas.

A DNS server can successfully resolve internal AD records while external DNS resolution is failing.

### 2. Active Directory depends on DNS.

Clients use DNS to locate Domain Controllers and Active Directory services.

### 3. DNS forwarding allows internal DNS servers to resolve external names.

```text
Internal DNS
      ↓
Unknown external name
      ↓
Forwarder
      ↓
External DNS
```

### 4. Troubleshoot in layers.

```text
IP
↓
Network
↓
DNS
↓
Active Directory
↓
Authentication
```

### 5. Don't make unnecessary changes.

First gather evidence, identify the likely cause, make an authorized change, verify the result, and document the resolution.

